            <ArticleTitle>Complications of spinal anesthesia.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>55-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Serious neurological complications after spinal anesthesia are rare, but do occur. The most common are postdural puncture headache and hypotension. Hypotension after spinal anesthesia is a physiological consequence of sympathetic blockade. The diagnoses and management of these sequelae are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
